 Small operations repository for the log retention job.
 
-`bin/archive-logs.sh SERVICE` packs the logs of one service from `logs/` into a dated
-tarball under `archives/`. It runs from cron on the log host every night.
+`bin/archive-logs.sh [--keep-days N] SERVICE [SERVICE...]` packs the logs of each named
+service from `logs/` into a dated tarball (`SERVICE-YYYYMMDD.tar.gz`) under `archives/`.
+It runs from cron on the log host every night.
 
-Archives are pruned by hand today.
+```
+bin/archive-logs.sh api web
+bin/archive-logs.sh --keep-days 30 api web
+```
+
+- Service names must match `^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9_-]{0,63}$` and have a directory under `logs/`.
+  Everything is validated before anything is written, and a service without logs fails the run
+  (exit 66; bad usage exits 64).
+- `--keep-days N` (N a positive integer) deletes archives in `archives/` older than N days,
+  by modification time. Pruning happens only after all new archives are in place, and not at all
+  if any archive failed. Without the option nothing is pruned.
+- On success it prints one summary line, for example
+  `archived 2 service(s): api web; pruned 3 archive(s) older than 30 days`.
+- Paths are resolved relative to the repository, so the working directory does not matter.
